<title>BRAZIL: Brazil portworkers return to job at Santos.</title>
<headline>Brazil portworkers return to job at Santos.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portworkers at Brazil's main port of Santos returned to their jobs at 0700 local/1000 GMT on Friday after holding a 24-hour work stoppage to protest delays in receiving their April salary, a union spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>&quot;Everybody is back. There is no strike,&quot; said a spokeswoman at the Santos Port Operators Union.</p>
<p>Workers stopped work on Thursday when the CODESP port authority deposited only 65 percent of workers' April salary. Later that day, the port authority paid the remaining 35 percent.</p>
<p>--John Miller, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248-5414</p>
</text>
